Q6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-19T15:51:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-19T15:55:12Z","body":"> The `reports_contacts()` condition disappeared, is it ok? Just sanity checking.\r\n\r\nYes! That was a remnant from the previous `sync_state` approach, to emulate the behavior of Godot Physics, where kinematic bodies that report contacts (i.e. a `RigidBody3D` frozen as kinematic) are never allowed to go to sleep and thus always have their state synchronization (and thus `_integrate_forces`) called.\r\n\r\nIt's not needed as of #100983, since we also prevent those types of bodies from going to sleep, meaning `JoltBody3D::pre_step` (and thus `_enqueue_call_queries`) will always be called on them.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2600919582/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2602819131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101803#issuecomment-2602819131","issue_url":"https: